From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: coop-fetch <coop-fetch@localhost>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:37:43 -0900
Subject: [PATCH] Co-op local co-op: Field of view 150% by default
 (HOS_FOV_DEFAULT)

For oot-remake-multiplayer's local co-op (row 325): several games on one
PC, each in a part of the screen (patch 0047: a half keeps the game's height
at about 8:9), looked zoomed in. fov_default: the Field of view a run
starts at where the player kept the Insert menu row's own 100%, through the
menu's env_override: never saved, so a game started alone is unchanged; a
Field of view the player chose stays theirs, and one changed in the menu
during the run is saved as theirs. host/oot_fov.c reads the row at each
gameplay camera update, so it takes effect without a restart.

Two callers, one rule: HOS_FOV_DEFAULT=<50..150> at the start (the co-op
kit's local co-op start sets 150 for each of its games), and the co-op
module's setting_set("field_of_view_default", 150) while the game runs, in
the game whose Local co-op page starts the others (it was already running,
so it had no HOS_FOV_DEFAULT).
---
 gpu/vk/vk_menu.cpp | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gpu/vk/vk_menu.cpp b/gpu/vk/vk_menu.cpp
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/gpu/vk/vk_menu.cpp
+++ b/gpu/vk/vk_menu.cpp
@@ -989,6 +989,20 @@ int saved_value(int* value) {
     }
     return *value;
 }
+/// (oot-remake-multiplayer, patch 0048, row 325) Local co-op's Field of view: `want` (50..150, on the row's steps of 5) for
+/// this run where the player kept the row's own 100%, as an environment override (env_override): never saved, so the
+/// options file keeps the player's own; a Field of view the player chose stays theirs, and one changed in the menu during
+/// the run is saved as theirs. One rule for both callers: HOS_FOV_DEFAULT at the start (menu_init) and the co-op
+/// module's "field_of_view_default" while the game runs (menu_setting_set: a game whose Local co-op page starts the
+/// others). host/oot_fov.c reads the row at each gameplay camera update (rx_option(HOS_OPT_FOV)): no restart.
+/// True when the row holds `want` now.
+bool fov_default(int want) {
+    const int v = std::min(std::max((want + 2) / 5 * 5, 50), 150);
+    if (opts.fov == v) return true;   // (already: an earlier start, or the player's own)
+    if (opts.fov != 100 || v == 100) return false;
+    env_override(&opts.fov, v);
+    return true;
+}
 } // namespace   // (#1633: asked by the modules too, menu_module.h's "what modules ask the renderer")
 /// The menu set the row (the player or a preset): its value is saved from now on, even where it is the
 /// one the environment forced
@@ -4508,6 +4522,10 @@ void menu_init() {
         player_custom_output = custom_output;   // (parse_output replaces the player's own size with the environment's)
         env_override(&opts.output_res, parse_output(e));
     }
+    // (HOS_FOV_DEFAULT=<50..150>: the Field of view this run starts at where the player kept the row's own 100% (fov_default).
+    // Co-op's local co-op start (several games on one PC, each in a part of the screen: oot-remake-multiplayer's kit,
+    // local-coop.ps1 Set-KitLocalEnvironment) sets 150, row 325. A game started alone gets none and is unchanged.)
+    if (const char* e = getenv("HOS_FOV_DEFAULT"); e && *e) fov_default(atoi(e));
     // (the FSR 4 model for this run: RX_VK_FSR4_MODEL over the saved row; the engine's live value follows the row)
     const int fsr4_env = fsr4_model_env();
     if (fsr4_env >= 0) env_override(&opts.fsr4_model, fsr4_env);
@@ -4958,6 +4976,20 @@ static bool bridge_key_is(const char* row_key, const char* key) {
 int menu_setting_set(const char* key, int value, MkwVkSetting* out) {
     bridge_probe_first();
     std::lock_guard lk(menu_mu);
+    // (oot-remake-multiplayer, patch 0048, row 325) "field_of_view_default": the Field of view row for this run only
+    // (fov_default: over the row's own 100% only, never saved), not a row of its own. The co-op module asks it in a game
+    // whose Local co-op page starts the other games, as HOS_FOV_DEFAULT does at a start. 1: the row holds it now (*out
+    // the Field of view row), -2: the player's own Field of view stays (left as it was).
+    if (key && !strcmp(key, "field_of_view_default")) {
+        if (!fov_default(value)) return -2;
+        menu_refresh = true;
+        for (int f = 0; f < (int)std::size(rows); f++)
+            if (rows[f].value == &opts.fov && bridge_row(f)) {
+                if (out) bridge_fill(f, out);
+                return 1;
+            }
+        return 1;
+    }
     int i = 0;
     while (i < (int)std::size(rows) && !(bridge_row(i) && bridge_key_is(ini_key(rows[i]), key))) i++;
     if (i == (int)std::size(rows)) return 0;
-- 
